<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!--
      No components are declared here any more, and that is deliberate.

      This plugin used to declare a foreground Service
      (CallRingtoneService, foregroundServiceType="phoneCall", later
      "shortService"). That service crashed the app in the field with
      ForegroundServiceDidNotStartInTimeException, because a foreground
      service must call startForeground() within seconds of being started
      or Android kills the whole process — a promise that is genuinely hard
      to keep here (Android 14+ service-type gating, notification ownership
      colliding with the notification flutter_local_notifications already
      posts, and start/stop races when a call is answered immediately).

      It is also unnecessary: RingtonePlayer plays the ringtone through
      android.media.Ringtone, which delegates to the system's remote
      ringtone player. The audio therefore comes out of the SYSTEM audio
      process, not ours, so our process needs no elevated priority to keep
      it playing — and no service, no notification of our own, and no
      permission beyond VIBRATE (already declared by the app).

      See RingtonePlayer.kt for the full reasoning.
    -->

</manifest>
